---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const interpretReadinessResult = await interpretReadiness(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const recoverCommitmentsResult = await recoverCommitments(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretReadinessResult.accepted);
const matchLotsResult = await matchLots(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, recoverCommitmentsResult.accepted);
const scheduleResourcesResult = await scheduleResources(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, matchLotsResult.accepted);
const replanDeliveryResult = await replanDelivery(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, scheduleResourcesResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { interpretReadiness: interpretReadinessResult, recoverCommitments: recoverCommitmentsResult, matchLots: matchLotsResult, scheduleResources: scheduleResourcesResult, replanDelivery: replanDeliveryResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...interpretReadinessResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...recoverCommitmentsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...matchLotsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...scheduleResourcesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...replanDeliveryResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...interpretReadinessResult.checks, ...recoverCommitmentsResult.checks, ...matchLotsResult.checks, ...scheduleResourcesResult.checks, ...replanDeliveryResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A grower revises expected quantity: preserve the prior estimate and recompute affected allocations. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve the prior estimate and recompute affected allocations.) through the existing stage result for HarvestReadiness; preserve exact source/version and the prior HarvestReadiness, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — Two varieties share a common name: retain exact variety and quality requirements. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (retain exact variety and quality requirements.) through the existing stage result for HarvestReadiness; preserve exact source/version and the prior HarvestReadiness, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — Equipment is available but an operator is not: treat both as constrained resources. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (treat both as constrained resources.) through the existing stage result for HarvestReadiness; preserve exact source/version and the prior HarvestReadiness, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A customer rejects a substitution: keep the original unmet commitment visible. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (keep the original unmet commitment visible.) through the existing stage result for HarvestReadiness; preserve exact source/version and the prior HarvestReadiness, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — Actual yield differs from plan: reconcile harvested, stored, and delivered quantities separately. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (reconcile harvested, stored, and delivered quantities separately.) through the existing stage result for HarvestReadiness; preserve exact source/version and the prior HarvestReadiness, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, interpretReadiness: interpretReadinessResult, recoverCommitments: recoverCommitmentsResult, matchLots: matchLotsResult, scheduleResources: scheduleResourcesResult, replanDelivery: replanDeliveryResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
